     "text": "```python\ndef is_valid_sudoku(board):\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if a given 9x9 Sudoku board is valid according to Sudoku rules.\n    The board is valid if:\n    - Each row contains the digits 1-9 without repetition.\n    - Each column contains the digits 1-9 without repetition.\n    - Each of the nine 3x3 subgrids contains the digits 1-9 without repetition.\n    - The board is a 9x9 grid.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Check if the board is a 9x9 grid\n    if len(board) != 9 or any(len(row) != 9 for row in board):\n        return False\n\n    # Check rows\n    for row in board:\n        seen = set()\n        for num in row:\n            if num != '.' and num in seen:\n                return False\n            if num != '.':\n                seen.add(num)\n\n    # Check columns\n    for col in range(9):\n        seen = set()\n        for row in range(9):\n            num = board[row][col]\n            if num != '.' and num in seen:\n                return False\n            if num != '.':\n                seen.add(num)\n\n    # Check 3x3 subgrids\n    for row_start in range(0, 9, 3):\n        for col_start in range(0, 9, 3):\n            seen = set()\n            for row in range(row_start, row_start + 3):\n                for col in range(col_start, col_start + 3):\n                    num = board[row][col]\n                    if num != '.' and num in seen:\n                        return False\n                    if num != '.':\n                        seen.add(num)\n\n    return True\n```",
