     "text": "```python\nwr_is_valid_sudoku = wr_is_valid_sudoku\ndef wr_is_valid_sudoku(grid: list[list[int]]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if a given 9x9 grid is a valid Sudoku board.\n\n    A Sudoku board is valid if:\n    1. Each row contains digits from 1 to 9 without repetition.\n    2. Each column contains digits from 1 to 9 without repetition.\n    3. Each of the nine 3x3 subgrids contains digits from 1 to 9 without repetition.\n    4. The grid is exactly 9x9 in size.\n\n    Args:\n        grid: A list of lists representing the 9x9 Sudoku grid.\n\n    Returns:\n        A boolean indicating whether the grid is valid.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(grid) != 9:\n        return False\n\n    for row in grid:\n        if len(row) != 9:\n            return False\n        if any(not isinstance(num, int) or num < 1 or num > 9 for num in row):\n            return False\n\n    for i in range(9):\n        for j in range(9):\n            if grid[i][j] != 0:\n                if grid[i][j] in grid[i] or grid[i][j] in [grid[x][j] for x in range(9)]:\n                    return False\n                subgrid_row, subgrid_col = 3 * (i // 3), 3 * (j // 3)\n                subgrid = [\n                    grid[subgrid_row + x][subgrid_col + y]\n                    for x in range(3)\n                    for y in range(3)\n                ]\n                if grid[i][j] in subgrid:\n                    return False\n\n    return True\n```",
